      text: "User prompt: Build a professional, premium, mobile-first e-commerce/catalog website for:\n\nBUSINESS NAME:\nPearls Elegance Thrift Abaya Wears\n\nBUSINESS TYPE:\nModest fashion / clothing store specializing in affordable thrift abayas, jalabiyas, modest dresses, and related women\'s and men\'s modest wear.\n\nLOCATION:\nIbadan Garage Side, Ijebu Ode, 120101, Ogun State, Nigeria\n\nPHONE / WHATSAPP:\n0811 244 4087\n\nWHATSAPP LINK:\nhttps://wa.me/2348112444087\n\nGOOGLE BUSINESS RATING:\n5.0 stars from 1 Google review.\nDo not exaggerate this rating or imply there are more reviews than currently available.\n\nCURRENT PRODUCTS / EXAMPLES:\n1. Thrift Tops and Gowns \342\200\224 \342\202\2462,000\n2. Kiddies Abaya and Jalabia \342\200\224 \342\202\2466,000\n3. Thrift Abaya Wears \342\200\224 \342\202\2469,000\n4. New arrivals may include adult jalabias around \342\202\2466,000\n5. New arrival abayas around \342\202\24612,000\n6. Thrift Kinomo abaya with new inner dress around \342\202\24610,000\342\200\223\342\202\24615,000\n\nBUSINESS DESCRIPTION:\nPearls Elegance Thrift Abaya Wears specializes in affordable thrift abayas, jalabiyas, and modest fashion for women and men. The business offers quality pieces with beautiful designs, embroidery, and colors at budget-friendly prices. They serve customers across Nigeria and provide wholesale and bulk purchase options for resellers and boutique owners. Their goal is to make elegant modest wear accessible while providing reliable service.\n\nWEBSITE OBJECTIVE:\nCreate a polished online storefront that:\n- Makes the brand look trustworthy and established\n- Clearly showcases available products\n- Makes it easy for customers to order through WhatsApp\n- Helps customers discover new arrivals\n- Clearly communicates that products are affordable thrift/modest fashion\n- Supports customers within Ijebu Ode and across Nigeria\n- Attracts both individual shoppers and wholesale/bulk buyers\n- Works exceptionally well on mobile devices\n\nDESIGN DIRECTION:\nCreate a sophisticated modest-fashion aesthetic.\n\nThe design should feel:\n- Elegant\n- Feminine\n- Clean\n- Premium\n- Warm\n- Modern\n- Trustworthy\n- Fashion-focused\n\nAvoid:\n- Generic templates\n- Excessive gradients\n- Neon colors\n- Cyberpunk styling\n- SaaS-style dashboards\n- Overly futuristic UI\n- Excessive animations\n- Cluttered layouts\n- Fake luxury branding\n\nCOLOR PALETTE:\nUse a refined neutral fashion palette such as:\n- Warm ivory / cream\n- Soft beige\n- Charcoal / deep black\n- Muted gold as a subtle accent\n- Very light warm gray\n\nUse color sparingly and maintain strong readability.\n\nTYPOGRAPHY:\nUse an elegant serif typeface for major headings paired with a clean modern sans-serif for body text and navigation.\n\nThe typography should communicate modest luxury without looking too expensive or inaccessible.\n\nBRAND FEEL:\nThink:\n\"Affordable elegance meets modest fashion.\"\n\nThe website should not make thrift clothing feel cheap.\nInstead, communicate:\nbeautiful pieces + affordability + modesty + convenience.\n\nSITE STRUCTURE:\n\n1. HOME PAGE\n\nHero section:\nCreate a visually strong fashion-focused hero section with high-quality abaya/modest-wear imagery.\n\nHeadline example:\n\"Elegant Modest Wear, Beautifully Within Reach.\"\n\nSupporting text:\n\"Discover affordable thrift abayas, jalabiyas, dresses, and modest fashion pieces for women, men, and kids.\"\n\nPrimary CTA:\n\"Shop Collection\"\n\nSecondary CTA:\n\"Order on WhatsApp\"\n\nInclude a small trust/location line:\n\"Based in Ijebu Ode, Ogun State \342\200\242 Delivering across Nigeria\"\n\nDo not use fake statistics.\n\nFeatured categories:\n- Abayas\n- Jalabiyas\n- Kiddies Wear\n- Thrift Tops & Gowns\n- New Arrivals\n- Wholesale / Bulk\n\nFeatured products section:\nDisplay real products from the information provided above with prices in Nigerian Naira.\n\nUse polished product cards containing:\n- Product image\n- Product name\n- Price\n- Availability status\n- \"View Product\"\n- \"Order on WhatsApp\"\n\nAdd a \"New Arrivals\" section.\n\nUse content inspired by the business\'s recent Google updates, such as:\n- New arrival abayas\n- Adult jalabias\n- Thrift Kinomo abayas\n- Ready-to-wear washed and neatly packed thrift pieces\n\nDo NOT invent specific products that have not been provided. The product catalog should be easy to edit later.\n\nAdd a \"Why Shop With Pearls Elegance?\" section with genuine benefits based on the provided business information:\n- Affordable modest fashion\n- Carefully selected thrift pieces\n- Washed, ironed, and neatly packed items where applicable\n- Individual and bulk purchasing\n- Nationwide customer service\n- Convenient WhatsApp ordering\n\nAdd a section for wholesale customers:\n\"Buying for Resale?\"\nExplain that wholesale and bulk purchase options are available for:\n- Resellers\n- Boutique owners\n- Fashion retailers\n\nCTA:\n\"Ask About Wholesale\"\n\nAdd a location section:\n\"Visit Our Store\"\nIbadan Garage Side, Ijebu Ode, Ogun State\n\nInclude:\n- Address\n- Phone number\n- WhatsApp button\n- Google Maps / directions button\n\nAdd a customer trust section.\nOnly display the verified current rating:\n\"5.0 \342\230\205 Google Rating\"\n\"1 Google review\"\n\nDo not fabricate additional testimonials or customer reviews.\n\n2. SHOP / COLLECTION PAGE\n\nCreate a clean product catalog.\n\nInclude:\n- Search\n- Category filters\n- Price filters\n- New Arrivals filter\n- Product availability\n\nProduct categories:\n- Abayas\n- Jalabiyas\n- Dresses\n- Kiddies Abaya\n- Kiddies Jalabia\n- Thrift Tops\n- Thrift Gowns\n- Kinomo\n- Modest Wear\n- Wholesale / Bulk\n\nEach product card should have:\n- Product image\n- Product title\n- Price\n- Category\n- Availability\n- WhatsApp ordering CTA\n\nSince thrift inventory can change frequently, structure the product system so products can easily be added, removed, marked sold out, or updated.\n\n3. PRODUCT DETAILS PAGE\n\nEach product should have:\n- Large product image gallery\n- Product name\n- Price\n- Product description\n- Available sizes if provided\n- Color if provided\n- Condition/details\n- Availability\n- \"Order on WhatsApp\" button\n\nThe WhatsApp button should automatically create a message such as:\n\n\"Hello Pearls Elegance, I\'m interested in [PRODUCT NAME] priced at [PRICE]. Is it still available?\"\n\nDo not collect payments directly unless a reliable payment integration is intentionally added later.\n\n4. ABOUT PAGE\n\nTell the story of Pearls Elegance Thrift Abaya Wears.\n\nFocus on:\n- Affordable modest fashion\n- Elegant designs\n- Thrift fashion\n- Accessibility\n- Customer service\n- Serving customers in Ijebu Ode and across Nigeria\n- Wholesale and bulk purchasing\n\nKeep the writing authentic and not overly corporate.\n\n5. WHOLESALE PAGE\n\nCreate a dedicated page for resellers and boutique owners.\n\nHeadline:\n\"Stock Your Store With Affordable Modest Fashion.\"\n\nExplain that Pearls Elegance supports:\n- Resellers\n- Boutique owners\n- Bulk buyers\n\nInclude a CTA:\n\"Contact Us on WhatsApp\"\n\nCreate a short inquiry form with:\n- Name\n- Business name\n- Phone number\n- Products interested in\n- Quantity needed\n- Message\n\nAlso provide direct WhatsApp ordering.\n\n6. NEW ARRIVALS PAGE\n\nThis should be visually prominent.\n\nCreate a fashion-forward grid where new products can easily be uploaded.\n\nInclude a label:\n\"Freshly Added\"\n\nProduct cards should support:\n- New badge\n- Price\n- Product type\n- Order button\n\n7. CONTACT PAGE\n\nInclude:\nPearls Elegance Thrift Abaya Wears\nIbadan Garage Side\nIjebu Ode, Ogun State, Nigeria\n\nPhone:\n0811 244 4087\n\nWhatsApp:\nhttps://wa.me/2348112444087\n\nInclude business location, contact CTA, and directions.\n\nNAVIGATION:\n\nDesktop:\nLogo | Home | Shop | New Arrivals | Wholesale | About | Contact | WhatsApp\n\nMobile:\nUse a clean hamburger navigation and a persistent WhatsApp/order button.\n\nAdd a sticky mobile CTA:\n\"Order on WhatsApp\"\n\nUSER EXPERIENCE:\n\nThe customer journey should be extremely simple:\n\nDiscover product\n\342\206\222 View product\n\342\206\222 Check price/details\n\342\206\222 Click WhatsApp\n\342\206\222 Send inquiry/order\n\nMake this especially easy for Nigerian mobile users.\n\nUse:\n- Fast page loading\n- Optimized images\n- Responsive layouts\n- Large tap targets\n- Clear pricing in \342\202\246\n- Simple navigation\n- Minimal unnecessary forms\n- Excellent mobile performance\n\nSEO:\n\nOptimize the website for searches around:\n- Abaya in Ijebu Ode\n- Thrift Abaya Ijebu Ode\n- Jalabiya in Ogun State\n- Modest wear Nigeria\n- Affordable Abaya Nigeria\n- Thrift fashion Ijebu Ode\n- Abaya and Jalabia Nigeria\n- Wholesale Abaya Nigeria\n\nUse appropriate:\n- Page titles\n- Meta descriptions\n- Heading hierarchy\n- Image alt text\n- Local business information\n- Product structured data where appropriate\n\nTECHNICAL REQUIREMENTS:\n\nBuild the website using a modern production-ready stack.\n\nPrioritize:\n- Clean reusable components\n- Maintainable code\n- Responsive design\n- Accessibility\n- SEO\n- Performance\n- Semantic HTML\n- Optimized images\n- Good Core Web Vitals\n\nPrepare the architecture so a product catalog can later be connected to a CMS/database without rebuilding the frontend.\n\nDo not add fake:\n- Reviews\n- Sales numbers\n- Customer counts\n- Years in business\n- Awards\n- Certifications\n- Testimonials\n- Social proof\n- Product availability\n\nUse only business information that has been provided.\n\nIMPORTANT:\nThis is a real Nigerian fashion business. Make the website feel authentic and commercially useful, not like a design concept.\n\nThe final design should feel like a premium independent modest-fashion brand with a strong local identity, while still being accessible to customers throughout Nigeria.\n\nAdd subtle micro-interactions and tasteful animations, but keep them restrained.\n\nThe final result should look polished enough to be presented as a professional website built by a serious web development agency.\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.3.3\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^6.1.1\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^8.3.0\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\n@types/react: ^19.3.0\n@types/react-dom: ^19.3.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.3.3\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ^7.0.2\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"types\": [\"vite/client\"],\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    }
  }
}
