    thinking: "**Defining Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve started by defining the core data structures needed for the application. Specifically, I\'ve created TypeScript definitions for `Product`, `Category`, `WholesaleInquiry`, `FilterState`, `OrderItem`, and `ReviewInfo` within `src/types.ts`. I\'m now working on populating `src/data/products.ts` with a real product list based on the \"Thrift Tops and Gowns\" specification.\n\n\n**Populating Product Data**\n\nI\'ve begun populating `src/data/products.ts`. I\'m integrating the provided price points and categories for items like \"Kiddies Abaya and Jalabia\", \"Thrift Abaya Wears\", \"New Arrival Abayas\", and more. I\'m also preparing for variants. I\'m focusing on accurately representing these products within the defined data structures, alongside the price points and categories I am provided.\n\n\n**Developing UI Components**\n\nI\'m currently focused on developing the key UI components. I am working on the responsive `Navbar` and `Footer`, including location, contact, and rating details. Additionally, I am designing a sticky mobile bottom bar, and polishing product cards with badges, prices, and WhatsApp order options. I am also working on `ProductDetailModal` which includes a gallery, condition, sizes, colors, and material details. I\'m also preparing to integrate a trust rating badge.\n\n\n"
