ers\n- persistent WhatsApp access\n\nThe sticky mobile bar should feel integrated into the brand, not like a generic app toolbar.\n\n==================================================\nIMAGE QUALITY\n==================================================\n\nEvery image should feel like it was professionally photographed.\n\nFor all product visuals:\n- Neutral studio backgrounds\n- Soft directional lighting\n- Clean garment presentation\n- Mannequin/dress-form presentation\n- Accurate garment colors\n- High resolution\n- Minimal distractions\n\nThe clothes must be the hero.\n\n==================================================\nIMPORTANT BRAND PRINCIPLE\n==================================================\n\nThis is NOT:\n\n\342\200\234a website for a thrift seller.\342\200\235\n\nIt should visually communicate:\n\n\342\200\234A modern modest-fashion brand that happens to offer affordable thrift pieces.\342\200\235\n\nThat distinction is extremely important.\n\nThe customer should immediately feel:\n\n\342\200\234This brand takes fashion seriously.\342\200\235\n\n==================================================\nFINAL QUALITY BAR\n==================================================\n\nBefore finishing, review every page as if the website were being presented to a client who paid \342\202\2461,000,000+ for the website.\n\nAsk:\n\nDoes this look professionally art-directed?\n\nDoes the typography feel premium?\n\nDo the clothes look desirable?\n\nDoes the photography feel consistent?\n\nDoes the spacing feel intentional?\n\nDoes the mobile version feel expensive?\n\nDoes anything look like an AI-generated template?\n\nDoes anything look cheap, generic, crowded, or unnecessary?\n\nRemove anything that lowers the perceived value.\n\nThe final result should look like a serious fashion-commerce website designed by a high-end digital agency.\n\nPreserve the existing functionality, product system, WhatsApp ordering, inquiry basket, SEO, and business information.\n\nUpgrade the E