    session_summary: "### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n*   **Final 10% Polish (Directive Section 18):** Perform a final, obsessive QA pass to ensure the \"exceptional engineering and design\" standard is met.\n    *   *Status:* IMPLEMENTATION (Final Polish Phase)\n    *   *Details:* The user explicitly requested a final pass to check for 1px alignment errors, inconsistent spacing, typography scale, line heights, icon sizing, button height, border treatment, corner radii, image cropping, hover behavior, focus states, sticky positioning, mobile spacing, section transitions, and any amateur design details.\n*   **Production-Ready Audit:** Ensure the site feels \"deliberately engineered, designed, tested, and refined\" rather than AI-generated.\n    *   *Status:* IMPLEMENTATION\n    *   *Details:* Remove any remaining \"AI-generated\" patterns (excessive rounded cards, generic gradients, glassmorphism, etc.).\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n\n*   **Design Philosophy:** The website must be \"Premium, Editorial, Minimal, Elegant, Modern, Warm, Sophisticated.\"\n*   **Photography Constraint:** \"Clothing MUST remain on mannequins / dress forms. NO human models.\"\n*   **Trust Constraint:** \"Do NOT use the Google rating/review section. Do NOT fabricate: reviews, testimonials, statistics, awards, customer counts, years in business, certifications, sales numbers.\"\n*   **Content Strategy:** \"Concise and confident\" copy. Avoid \"large blocks of generic marketing text.\"\n*   **Technical Philosophy:** \"High-quality engineering does NOT mean adding complexity.\" Use the simplest architecture that provides a robust, production-quality result.\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n\n*   **Accessibility & UX Polish:**\n    *   `ProductDetailModal.tsx`: Implemented body scroll locking, keyboard `Escape` key handling, and added necessary ARIA attributes (`role=\"dialog\"`, `aria-modal=\"true\"`) to ensure professional-grade modal behavior.\n    *   `InquiryDrawer.tsx`: Implemented body scroll locking, keyboard `Escape` key handling, and added necessary ARIA attributes to ensure professional-grade drawer behavior.\n*   **Design System Overhaul:** Standardized typography (Cormorant Garamond for headlines, Plus Jakarta Sans for body), spacing, and color palette (`#FAF8F5`, `#1C1917`, `#C5A059`).\n*   **Removal of Fake Social Proof:** Completely purged Google reviews, fake ratings, and fabricated trust badges from `ContactView.tsx`, `index.html`, and all components.\n*   **Homepage Editorial Rhythm:** Restructured the homepage to follow a storytelling flow: Editorial Hero \342\206\222 New Arrivals \342\206\222 Curated Collections \342\206\222 Brand Statement \342\206\222 Selected Products \342\206\222 Customer Testimonials \342\206\222 Wholesale \342\206\222 Store Location \342\206\222 Final CTA.\n*   **WhatsApp Integration:** Refined the inquiry basket and WhatsApp ordering flow to feel like a first-class commerce feature, supporting multiple products and clear, pre-filled messaging.\n*   **Responsive UX:** Audited and refined mobile behavior (320px\342\200\223430px+) for all components, including the sticky mobile bar and inquiry drawer.\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n\n*   **Architecture:** The application is a React SPA with centralized state management in `App.tsx`.\n    *   `App.tsx` manages the `inquiryItems` state (persisted to `localStorage`) and handles routing between views (`HomeView`, `ShopView`, etc.).\n*   **Styling:** Tailwind CSS is used throughout. The design relies on a consistent spacing scale and color palette defined in `src/index.css`.\n*   **Accessibility Patterns:** Modals and drawers now include `useEffect` hooks to lock `document.body.style.overflow` and listen for `keydown` events to provide a native, polished feel.\n*   **WhatsApp Flow:** The `utils/whatsapp.ts` generates pre-filled messages. The inquiry drawer compiles these into a single message for the seller.\n*   **Constraints:** Avoided adding unnecessary dependencies or complex state management libraries. Kept the architecture simple to ensure performance and maintainability.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n\n*   **Edited Files:**\n    *   `/src/components/ProductDetailModal.tsx`: Added accessibility features (scroll locking, Escape key listener, ARIA attributes).\n    *   `/src/components/InquiryDrawer.tsx`: Added accessibility features (scroll locking, Escape key listener, ARIA attributes).\n*   **Viewed Files (Relevant for next steps):**\n    *   `/src/components/StickyMobileBar.tsx`: Contains the mobile CTA logic.\n    *   `/src/views/ShopView.tsx`: Main catalog view with filtering logic.\n    *   `/src/views/WholesaleView.tsx`: Wholesale inquiry form and information.\n    *   `/src/views/AboutView.tsx`: Brand story and values.\n    *   `/src/views/NewArrivalsView.tsx`: New arrivals display.\n    *   `/src/data/products.ts`: Static product data and business info.\n    *   `/src/utils/whatsapp.ts`: WhatsApp URL generation logic.\n    *   `/index.html`: SEO and metadata.\n    *   `/src/index.css`: Global styles and Tailwind theme configuration.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n*   **Immediate Next Step:** Continue the \"Final 10% Polish\" pass.\n    *   Review the site at all breakpoints (320px, 375px, 768px, 1024px, 1440px) to ensure no 1px alignment issues or awkward spacing.\n    *   Verify that all hover states, focus states, and transitions feel intentional and premium.\n    *   Check for any remaining \"AI-generated\" artifacts (e.g., generic rounded corners, excessive shadows).\n*   **Context for Next Agent:** The site is in a \"final polish\" state. Do not rewrite core architecture. Focus on visual refinement and UX consistency. The user\'s directive (provided in the previous turn) is the primary source of truth for the \"exceptional\" standard required."
