    session_summary: "### 1. Outstanding User Requests\n\n*   **Final 10% Polish (Directive Section 18):** Perform a final, obsessive QA pass to ensure the \"exceptional engineering and design\" standard is met.\n    *   *Status:* **IMPLEMENTATION (Final Polish Phase)**\n    *   *Details:* The user requested a final pass to ensure 1px alignment, consistent spacing, and premium feel. The site is currently in this state.\n*   **Agency Credit:** Add \"Designed & Engineered by Namaco Technology Nigeria Limited\" subtly in the footer and About page.\n    *   *Status:* **COMPLETED**\n*   **Header Refinement:** Remove the top announcement bar and refine header spacing/proportions.\n    *   *Status:* **COMPLETED**\n\n### 2. User Knowledge\n\n*   **Design Philosophy:** \"Premium, Editorial, Minimal, Elegant, Modern, Warm, Sophisticated.\"\n*   **Photography Constraint:** \"Clothing MUST remain on mannequins / dress forms. NO human models.\"\n*   **Trust Constraint:** \"Do NOT use the Google rating/review section. Do NOT fabricate: reviews, testimonials, statistics, awards, customer counts, years in business, certifications, sales numbers.\"\n*   **Agency Credit:** \"Designed & Engineered by Namaco Technology Nigeria Limited.\" Must be subtle, professional, and not compete with the primary brand.\n*   **Header/UI Philosophy:** \"LESS UI, MORE FASHION, MORE WHITESPACE, MORE CONFIDENCE.\" No announcement bars, tickers, or promotional strips.\n\n### 3. Work Accomplished\n\n*   **Header Overhaul:** Removed the top announcement bar from `Navbar.tsx` and cleaned up associated CSS/logic. Refined header spacing and proportions to ensure a clean, premium mobile and desktop experience.\n*   **Agency Credit Implementation:** Added the required agency credit to `Footer.tsx` and `AboutView.tsx` with understated styling.\n*   **Homepage Editorial Rhythm:**\n    *   Added a \"Brand Statement\" section to `HomeView.tsx` to reinforce the value proposition.\n    *   Added a \"Final Editorial Call to Action\" section to `HomeView.tsx` to conclude the user journey.\n*   **Accessibility & UX Polish:**\n    *   `SearchModal.tsx`: Implemented body scroll locking, keyboard `Escape` key handling, and ARIA attributes.\n    *   `InquiryDrawer.tsx`: Implemented body scroll locking, keyboard `Escape` key handling, and ARIA attributes.\n*   **Design System:** Standardized typography (Cormorant Garamond/Plus Jakarta Sans), spacing, and color palette (`#FAF8F5`, `#1C1917`, `#C5A059`).\n\n### 4. Model Knowledge\n\n*   **Architecture:** React SPA with centralized state in `App.tsx` (manages `inquiryItems`).\n*   **Styling:** Tailwind CSS. Theme variables (colors, fonts) are defined in `/src/index.css`.\n*   **Navigation:** `onNavigate` prop in components triggers view changes and scrolls to top.\n*   **WhatsApp Flow:** `utils/whatsapp.ts` generates pre-filled messages.\n*   **Constraints:** No complex state management libraries; keep architecture simple for performance and maintainability.\n\n### 5. Files and Code\n\n*   **Edited Files:**\n    *   `/src/components/InquiryDrawer.tsx`: Added accessibility features.\n    *   `/src/components/SearchModal.tsx`: Added accessibility features.\n    *   `/src/views/HomeView.tsx`: Added Brand Statement and Final CTA sections.\n    *   `/src/components/Footer.tsx`: Added agency credit.\n    *   `/src/views/AboutView.tsx`: Added agency credit note.\n    *   `/src/components/Navbar.tsx`: Removed announcement bar, refined header layout.\n*   **Viewed Files (Relevant for next steps):**\n    *   `/src/index.css`: Defines the design system (colors, fonts).\n    *   `/src/data/products.ts`: Contains business info and WhatsApp URL.\n\n### 6. Current Work and Next Steps\n\n*   **Current State:** The website is in a \"final polish\" state. All major structural requests (header removal, agency credit, editorial flow) have been implemented.\n*   **Next Steps:**\n    *   Perform a final visual QA pass across all breakpoints (320px, 375px, 768px, 1024px, 1440px).\n    *   Verify that the removal of the announcement bar has not introduced any layout shifts or alignment issues in the hero section.\n    *   Check for any remaining \"AI-generated\" artifacts (e.g., generic rounded corners, excessive shadows) and refine them to match the \"Editorial Fashion\" aesthetic.\n    *   The next agent should focus on visual refinement and UX consistency rather than architectural changes."
