  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing WhatsApp Message Formatting**\n\nOkay, I\'ve started analyzing the specific WhatsApp message formatting requirements. I\'m focusing on how the message should automatically incorporate the exact product a customer is viewing. I need to figure out how to dynamically insert the product details into the message body when the customer clicks the \"ORDER ON WHATSAPP\" button. The example provided shows a simple \"Hello\" starter, which means the next data input is the product information.\n\n\n**Refining WhatsApp Message Templates**\n\nI\'m now refining the WhatsApp message templates within `src/utils/whatsapp.ts`. I\'m focusing on crafting a clean editorial structure with precise newlines and dynamic encoding. Specifically, I\'m updating `getProductWhatsAppUrl` and `getCombinedInquiryWhatsAppUrl` to align with the provided formatting, ensuring accurate product information insertion.\n\n\n**Implementing Dynamic Message Composition**\n\nI\'ve just implemented the dynamic message composition logic within the functions.  I am building the exact WhatsApp messages now using `getProductWhatsAppUrl` and `getCombinedInquiryWhatsAppUrl`. These functions correctly incorporate all relevant details, including product names, prices, quantities, and selected sizes or colors. I\'m satisfied that these functions address the need to generate formatted messages that automatically adapt to user input and product information.\n\n\n**Finalizing Order Inquiry Structure**\n\nI\'ve finalized the structure for combined order inquiries, ensuring comprehensive product details are included. The formatted messages in `getProductWhatsAppUrl` and `getCombinedInquiryWhatsAppUrl` now incorporate product names, prices, quantities, and variations effectively. I\'ve added a final prompt to confirm availability and express gratitude. The messages are dynamically generated and properly encoded for WhatsApp. I am now proceeding to finalize the button labeling as specified.\n\n\n**Optimizing Button Integration**\n\nI\'m now integrating the WhatsApp button more effectively, focusing on visibility. By changing the button on the `ProductCard` to bright green with \"Order on WhatsApp,\" I\'m making the primary order flow more apparent. I\'ve noted that the button is also present in `ProductDetailModal.tsx`. I believe the placement and color are key to improving the user experience and encouraging direct orders via WhatsApp.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 471377331
    }
