steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1789902513
      nanos: 666544785
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
    source_trajectory_step_info {
      trajectory_id: "4f917d54-c553-47b5-92e6-7ba603c32a73"
      step_index: 111
      metadata_index: 250
      cascade_id: "4f917d54-c553-47b5-92e6-7ba603c32a73"
    }
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "FINAL PRE-EXPORT PRODUCTION AUDIT\n\nDo NOT redesign the website yet.\n\nI want you to perform a complete final audit of the current Pearls Elegance Thrift Abaya Wears website and determine whether it is genuinely ready to be exported and deployed.\n\nTreat this as a professional pre-launch QA review by:\n- Principal Frontend Engineer\n- Senior UI/UX Designer\n- QA Engineer\n- Performance Engineer\n- SEO Engineer\n\nInspect the actual current codebase and running application.\n\nDO NOT assume something works just because it exists in the code.\n\nTest and verify it.\n\n==================================================\n1. FUNCTIONALITY\n==================================================\n\nVerify that all major functionality actually works:\n\n- Homepage navigation\n- Desktop navigation\n- Mobile navigation\n- Search\n- Product filtering\n- Product sorting\n- Product availability states\n- Product detail pages\n- New Arrivals\n- Category pages/filters\n- Inquiry Basket\n- Add to Inquiry\n- Remove from Inquiry\n- Multi-product inquiry\n- WhatsApp ordering\n- Product-specific WhatsApp messages\n- Contact buttons\n- Phone/call links\n- Location/directions link\n- Forms\n- Footer links\n\nFor WhatsApp, verify that clicking a specific product\'s \342\200\234Order on WhatsApp\342\200\235 generates a message containing THAT EXACT PRODUCT NAME and PRICE.\n\nVerify that the multi-product inquiry correctly includes all selected products.\n\n==================================================\n2. CONTENT ACCURACY\n==================================================\n\nVerify the website contains only supported business information.\n\nBusiness:\n\nPearls Elegance Thrift Abaya Wears\n\nAddress:\n\nIbadan Garage Side, Ijebu Ode, 120101, Ogun State, Nigeria\n\nPhone:\n\n0811 244 4087\n\nWhatsApp:\n\n2348112444087\n\nMake sure there are NO unsupported or fabricated:\n- reviews\n- ratings\n- testimonials\n- statistics\n- awards\n- certifications\n- years of experience\n- customer counts\n- opening hours\n- delivery guarantees\n- product claims\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe Google review/rating section was intentionally removed.\n\nVerify that there are NO remaining visible references to:\n- Google Rating\n- Google Reviews\n- 5.0 Google rating\n- 1 Google review\n- Google review badges\n\n==================================================\n3. HEADER\n==================================================\n\nVerify that the old announcement bar is completely removed.\n\nSearch the codebase for all remaining:\n- announcement bar components\n- ticker logic\n- announcement styles\n- unused announcement data\n- related imports\n\nVerify that removing it has NOT created:\n- empty gaps\n- excessive margin\n- excessive padding\n- broken positioning\n- layout shifts\n\nHeader must work correctly on all screen sizes.\n\n==================================================\n4. RESPONSIVE QA\n==================================================\n\nTest the application at:\n\n320px\n360px\n375px\n390px\n430px\n768px\n1024px\n1280px\n1440px\n\nLook specifically for:\n- horizontal scrolling\n- clipped content\n- overlapping elements\n- broken grids\n- text overflow\n- broken typography\n- sticky footer/header problems\n- inquiry drawer issues\n- navigation problems\n- buttons extending outside containers\n- incorrect image cropping\n- excessive whitespace\n- insufficient whitespace\n\nThe website should feel intentionally designed at every breakpoint.\n\n==================================================\n5. VISUAL QA\n==================================================\n\nReview every page visually.\n\nCheck:\n- typography consistency\n- spacing consistency\n- alignment\n- button consistency\n- card consistency\n- image quality\n- image ratios\n- colors\n- shadows\n- borders\n- corner radii\n- section rhythm\n- responsive composition\n\nMake sure clothing is presented on mannequins/dress forms rather than human models.\n\nIdentify anything that still looks:\n- generic\n- unfinished\n- cheap\n- inconsistent\n- AI-generated\n- overly decorative\n- unnecessarily complicated\n\nDo NOT make subjective redesign changes during this audit.\n\nJust identify actual issues.\n\n==================================================\n6. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nAudit:\n- image sizes\n- image loading\n- lazy loading\n- font loading\n- JavaScript bundle\n- unnecessary dependencies\n- unnecessary re-renders\n- layout shifts\n- animation performance\n\nLook for obvious performance problems that could hurt mobile users.\n\n==================================================\n7. ACCESSIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n- semantic HTML\n- keyboard navigation\n- focus states\n- accessible buttons\n- form labels\n- image alt text\n- color contrast\n- touch target sizes\n- drawer/modal accessibility\n\n==================================================\n8. SEO\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n- title tags\n- meta descriptions\n- H1 hierarchy\n- canonical URLs\n- Open Graph metadata\n- favicon\n- robots.txt\n- sitemap\n- structured data\n\nCheck that there are no obvious SEO errors.\n\n==================================================\n9. CODE QUALITY\n==================================================\n\nInspect the source for:\n- console errors\n- console warnings\n- broken imports\n- unused imports\n- dead components\n- dead CSS\n- duplicated logic\n- obvious bugs\n- hardcoded fragile behavior\n- missing error handling\n\nDo NOT perform unnecessary refactoring.\n\nOnly flag issues that matter for production readiness.\n\n==================================================\n10. SECURITY / CONFIGURATION\n==================================================\n\nCheck for obvious frontend security or configuration problems.\n\nMake sure:\n- no secrets are exposed\n- no private API keys are hardcoded\n- environment variables are handled correctly\n- external links are valid\n- WhatsApp URL construction is safe\n- user input is handled appropriately\n\n==================================================\n11. FINAL PRODUCTION CHECK\n==================================================\n\nDetermine whether the website is ready to export.\n\nUse exactly these categories:\n\n\342\234\205 READY\n\342\232\240\357\270\217 NEEDS MINOR FIXES\n\342\235\214 NOT READY\n\nThen provide:\n\nA. OVERALL STATUS\n\nB. BLOCKING ISSUES\nIssues that MUST be fixed before export.\n\nC. NON-BLOCKING ISSUES\nThings that can be improved later without preventing export.\n\nD. VERIFIED WORKING\nList the major features you actually tested successfully.\n\nE. FINAL EXPORT CHECKLIST\nA concise checklist of what must be true before export.\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nDo NOT tell me \342\200\234looks good\342\200\235 based only on inspection.\n\nActually inspect the code and test the application.\n\nDo NOT change the website during this audit unless you find a critical issue that can be safely fixed without altering the design direction.\n\nAt the end, give me a clear answer:\n\n\342\200\234READY TO EXPORT\342\200\235\n\nor\n\n\342\200\234NOT READY TO EXPORT\342\200\235\n\nbased on the actual audit results."
    items {
      text: "FINAL PRE-EXPORT PRODUCTION AUDIT\n\nDo NOT redesign the website yet.\n\nI want you to perform a complete final audit of the current Pearls Elegance Thrift Abaya Wears website and determine whether it is genuinely ready to be exported and deployed.\n\nTreat this as a professional pre-launch QA review by:\n- Principal Frontend Engineer\n- Senior UI/UX Designer\n- QA Engineer\n- Performance Engineer\n- SEO Engineer\n\nInspect the actual current codebase and running application.\n\nDO NOT assume something works just because it exists in the code.\n\nTest and verify it.\n\n==================================================\n1. FUNCTIONALITY\n==================================================\n\nVerify that all major functionality actually works:\n\n- Homepage navigation\n- Desktop navigation\n- Mobile navigation\n- Search\n- Product filtering\n- Product sorting\n- Product availability states\n- Product detail pages\n- New Arrivals\n- Category pages/filters\n- Inquiry Basket\n- Add to Inquiry\n- Remove from Inquiry\n- Multi-product inquiry\n- WhatsApp ordering\n- Product-specific WhatsApp messages\n- Contact buttons\n- Phone/call links\n- Location/directions link\n- Forms\n- Footer links\n\nFor WhatsApp, verify that clicking a specific product\'s \342\200\234Order on WhatsApp\342\200\235 generates a message containing THAT EXACT PRODUCT NAME and PRICE.\n\nVerify that the multi-product inquiry correctly includes all selected products.\n\n==================================================\n2. CONTENT ACCURACY\n==================================================\n\nVerify the website contains only supported business information.\n\nBusiness:\n\nPearls Elegance Thrift Abaya Wears\n\nAddress:\n\nIbadan Garage Side, Ijebu Ode, 120101, Ogun State, Nigeria\n\nPhone:\n\n0811 244 4087\n\nWhatsApp:\n\n2348112444087\n\nMake sure there are NO unsupported or fabricated:\n- reviews\n- ratings\n- testimonials\n- statistics\n- awards\n- certifications\n- years of experience\n- customer counts\n- opening hours\n- delivery guarantees\n- product claims\n\nIMPORTANT:\n\nThe Google review/rating section was intentionally removed.\n\nVerify that there are NO remaining visible references to:\n- Google Rating\n- Google Reviews\n- 5.0 Google rating\n- 1 Google review\n- Google review badges\n\n==================================================\n3. HEADER\n==================================================\n\nVerify that the old announcement bar is completely removed.\n\nSearch the codebase for all remaining:\n- announcement bar components\n- ticker logic\n- announcement styles\n- unused announcement data\n- related imports\n\nVerify that removing it has NOT created:\n- empty gaps\n- excessive margin\n- excessive padding\n- broken positioning\n- layout shifts\n\nHeader must work correctly on all screen sizes.\n\n==================================================\n4. RESPONSIVE QA\n==================================================\n\nTest the application at:\n\n320px\n360px\n375px\n390px\n430px\n768px\n1024px\n1280px\n1440px\n\nLook specifically for:\n- horizontal scrolling\n- clipped content\n- overlapping elements\n- broken grids\n- text overflow\n- broken typography\n- sticky footer/header problems\n- inquiry drawer issues\n- navigation problems\n- buttons extending outside containers\n- incorrect image cropping\n- excessive whitespace\n- insufficient whitespace\n\nThe website should feel intentionally designed at every breakpoint.\n\n==================================================\n5. VISUAL QA\n==================================================\n\nReview every page visually.\n\nCheck:\n- typography consistency\n- spacing consistency\n- alignment\n- button consistency\n- card consistency\n- image quality\n- image ratios\n- colors\n- shadows\n- borders\n- corner radii\n- section rhythm\n- responsive composition\n\nMake sure clothing is presented on mannequins/dress forms rather than human models.\n\nIdentify anything that still looks:\n- generic\n- unfinished\n- cheap\n- inconsistent\n- AI-generated\n- overly decorative\n- unnecessarily complicated\n\nDo NOT make subjective redesign changes during this audit.\n\nJust identify actual issues.\n\n==================================================\n6. PERFORMANCE\n==================================================\n\nAudit:\n- image sizes\n- image loading\n- lazy loading\n- font loading\n- JavaScript bundle\n- unnecessary dependencies\n- unnecessary re-renders\n- layout shifts\n- animation performance\n\nLook for obvious performance problems that could hurt mobile users.\n\n==================================================\n7. ACCESSIBILITY\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n- semantic HTML\n- keyboard navigation\n- focus states\n- accessible buttons\n- form labels\n- image alt text\n- color contrast\n- touch target sizes\n- drawer/modal accessibility\n\n==================================================\n8. SEO\n==================================================\n\nVerify:\n- title tags\n- meta descriptions\n- H1 hierarchy\n- canonical URLs\n- Open Graph metadata\n- favicon\n- robots.txt\n- sitemap\n- structured data\n\nCheck that there are no obvious SEO errors.\n\n==================================================\n9. CODE QUALITY\n==================================================\n\nInspect the source for:\n- console errors\n- console warnings\n- broken imports\n- unused imports\n- dead components\n- dead CSS\n- duplicated logic\n- obvious bugs\n- hardcoded fragile behavior\n- missing error handling\n\nDo NOT perform unnecessary refactoring.\n\nOnly flag issues that matter for production readiness.\n\n==================================================\n10. SECURITY / CONFIGURATION\n==================================================\n\nCheck for obvious frontend security or configuration problems.\n\nMake sure:\n- no secrets are exposed\n- no private API keys are hardcoded\n- environment variables are handled correctly\n-